{"title":"2022 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Complement)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Complement)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Fakesolve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Fakesolve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Fakesolve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Fakesolve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Fakesolve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Fakesolve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(⚡️Just_4_min⚡️)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (⚡️Just 4 min⚡️)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A pair of fair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided dice is rolled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> times. What is the least value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that the probability that the sum of the numbers face up on a roll equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> at least once is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cff4535f4252c03431c79fd1638208e478a32971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Complement.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Complement)\">Solution 1 (Complement)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Complement)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rolling a pair of fair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided dice, the probability of getting a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a1178ff284c4dc12fd4eb108256e10c32dea3038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac16:$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> Regardless what the first die shows, the second die has exactly one outcome to make the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b17ce6fcb2994d4241d780dd5311d828db133411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> We consider the complement: The probability of not getting a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/8/3c866d0176c44d9ea4b981b4818f30b2cb59c8a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac16=\\frac56.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" /> Rolling the pair of dice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> times, the probability of getting a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> at least once is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/3/7232ac1e9704f303b92a18b4ed8de4e562c2377c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"86\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/5162420461a253811c229d7d85dfd33a4c2e28aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n&gt;\\frac12,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"124\" height=\"46\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3beeaf60f532a4a413cc78ec502a30231b3f28c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n&lt;\\frac12.\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"43\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f64302d453dd56ab992cf1831c577b680db3b7d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac56\\right)^4&lt;\\frac12&lt;\\left(\\frac56\\right)^3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"165\" height=\"48\" /> the least integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying the inequality is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a953664a8aea1dbb6818844e3910c64cfa59d3e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Fakesolve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Fakesolve)\">Solution 2 (Fakesolve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Fakesolve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's try the answer choices. We can quickly find that when we roll <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dice, either the first and second sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the first and third sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or the second and third sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways for the first and second dice to sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways for the first and third to sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways for the second and third dice to sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, we overcounted (but not by much) so we can assume that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c8c609210637bb6d23ea44a6bdb675cb2fff0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(C) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Arcticturn\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Fakesolve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Fakesolve)\">Solution 3 (Fakesolve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Fakesolve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can start by figuring out what the probability is for each die to add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if there is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> roll. We can quickly see that the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8b7dd31c63b399cd72fe186a628adba5df3cad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, as there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers on a die, and there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways to add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers on a die. And since each time we roll the dice, we are adding to the probability, we can conclude that the total probability for rolling a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> rolls would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8b7dd31c63b399cd72fe186a628adba5df3cad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. The smallest number that satisfies this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c8c609210637bb6d23ea44a6bdb675cb2fff0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(C) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~mihikamishra\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Fakesolve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Fakesolve)\">Solution 4 (Fakesolve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Fakesolve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On each roll, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/337176718520f1f13185f020dff6ffc997f9f1f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> chance of rolling a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. You would need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of these rolls to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c58cd73bb719bb66764dfff773c96435f9ce11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot \\frac 16,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"38\" /> which is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/774818dd0dd86e52939dbd2b46f8c4cde68e3bc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c01a895fa636bc6618885c3b6368fedf5e7d88ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(C) }4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~dbnl\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.E2.9A.A1.EF.B8.8FJust_4_min.E2.9A.A1.EF.B8.8F.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(⚡️Just_4_min⚡️)\">Video Solution (⚡️Just 4 min⚡️)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (⚡️Just 4 min⚡️)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rYyb3NCWBXk\">https://youtu.be/rYyb3NCWBXk</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qT0hVzy7zeY\">https://youtu.be/qT0hVzy7zeY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Mi2AxPhnRno?t=207\">https://youtu.be/Mi2AxPhnRno?t=207</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Ani_lytical\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gFNsXRTETn0?s